    {
     "backBody": "<p>Examples of threats to the LAN include:</p><ul><li>Unauthorized access to wiring closets, data centers and computer rooms</li><li>Unauthorized access to systems, applications and data</li><li>Network operating system or software vulnerabilities and updates</li><li>Rogue users gaining unauthorized access to wireless networks</li><li>Exploits of data in transit</li><li>Having LAN servers with different hardware or operating systems makes managing and troubleshooting them more difficult</li><li>Unauthorized network probing and port scanning</li><li>Misconfigured firewalls</li></ul><p style=\"text-align:right\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\"><i class=\"fa fa-undo\"> </i>&nbsp;</span></p>",
     "backTitle": "",
     "frontImage": {
      "alt": "LAN written in the center of a circle surrounded by four devices linked by dotted lines: desktop with a bug on the screen, a tablet with a red triangle and exclamation mark, a smartphone with twelve colored tiles on the screen and a server",
      "src": "en-US/assets/fc9b9710e86b44ccb8306ccc3ed71501.png"
     },
     "_flipDirection": "horizontal",
     "_index": 0,
     "_parentId": "63ac1f7a231f0402b0232a78"
    }
